From: W4HO <87742609+W4HO-ham@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 13:18:57 -0647
Subject: [PATCH] PCI: dwc: gs201-cp: add a doorbell access under the link lock

The modem driver writes the doorbell into the modem's BAR window and
reads it back, retrying every millisecond for up to 100 ms while the
read returns all ones. It checks the link first, but the modem can ask
for the link to go down between the check and the access, and the
retry loop spans that window. Once the PHY is powered down (and on
gs201 isolated), an access to the window can hang the SoC.

Add gs201_pcie_cp_doorbell(): the write and the read-back under
cfg_lock, the lock cp_link_down() takes to clear cfg_ep_ok before it
touches PERST#, the PHY or the isolation, refused once the endpoint is
unreachable. The access itself is the modem driver's, unchanged, as
stock does it on both SoCs.

This changes the Pixel 7 Pro too: every doorbell there now goes through
cfg_lock and is held back while the endpoint is unreachable. That is
right on gs201 as well, where a read of the modem's window with the link
powered down hung the SoC (watchdog reset, nothing in pstore). Stock
serializes the doorbell against a link power-off one level up: Google's
cpif rings it under mc->pcie_tx_lock in pcie_send_ap2cp_irq()
(link_device.c), and s5100_poweroff_pcie() (modem_ctrl_s5100.c) takes
that lock to wait out a doorbell in flight before it powers the link
off. Here the link-down the CP asks for runs in the controller driver,
so the lock is the controller's.

Signed-off-by: W4HO <87742609+W4HO-ham@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-gs201-cp.c | 38 ++++++++++++++++++++++
 include/linux/soc/google/gs201-pcie-cp.h   |  3 ++
 2 files changed, 41 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-gs201-cp.c b/drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-gs201-cp.c
index 30eae683a..1d1cacce4 100644
--- a/drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-gs201-cp.c
+++ b/drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-gs201-cp.c
@@ -1619,6 +1619,44 @@ bool gs201_pcie_cp_link_ok(void)
 }
 EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(gs201_pcie_cp_link_ok);
 
+/**
+ * gs201_pcie_cp_doorbell() - write the modem's doorbell and read it back
+ * @addr: the doorbell register in the modem's BAR window (ioremapped)
+ * @val: the interrupt number to ring
+ * @readback: the register's value after the write
+ *
+ * The BAR window is reachable only while the endpoint is (link up, iATU
+ * set), and an access while the PHY is isolated or powered down can hang
+ * the SoC. The modem driver checks the link before it writes, but the CP
+ * can ask for the link to go down between its check and its access, and
+ * its read-back loop on the register (a millisecond per try, up to 100)
+ * spans that window. cfg_lock serializes the access against
+ * cp_link_down(), which clears cfg_ep_ok under it before it touches
+ * PERST#, the PHY or the isolation.
+ *
+ * Return: 0, -ENODEV before probe, -ENOLINK while the endpoint is not
+ * reachable (the caller reserves the doorbell for the next link up).
+ */
+int gs201_pcie_cp_doorbell(void __iomem *addr, u32 val, u32 *readback)
+{
+	struct gs201_pcie_cp *cp = READ_ONCE(gs201_cp);
+	unsigned long flags;
+	int ret = -ENOLINK;
+
+	if (!cp)
+		return -ENODEV;
+	raw_spin_lock_irqsave(&cp->cfg_lock, flags);
+	if (cp->cfg_ep_ok) {
+		writel(val, addr);
+		*readback = readl(addr);
+		ret = 0;
+	}
+	raw_spin_unlock_irqrestore(&cp->cfg_lock, flags);
+
+	return ret;
+}
+EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(gs201_pcie_cp_doorbell);
+
 /**
  * gs201_pcie_cp_check_msi_addr() - check the modem driver's MSI target
  * @addr: the MSI page the modem driver expects
diff --git a/include/linux/soc/google/gs201-pcie-cp.h b/include/linux/soc/google/gs201-pcie-cp.h
index 015f37993..2e37df02a 100644
--- a/include/linux/soc/google/gs201-pcie-cp.h
+++ b/include/linux/soc/google/gs201-pcie-cp.h
@@ -34,6 +34,7 @@ struct gs201_pcie_cp_event {
 int gs201_pcie_cp_poweron(unsigned int speed);
 void gs201_pcie_cp_poweroff(void);
 bool gs201_pcie_cp_link_ok(void);
+int gs201_pcie_cp_doorbell(void __iomem *addr, u32 val, u32 *readback);
 int gs201_pcie_cp_check_msi_addr(u64 addr);
 int gs201_pcie_cp_register_queue(irq_handler_t handler, void *ctx, int *irq);
 void gs201_pcie_cp_set_perst_level(int level);
@@ -49,6 +50,8 @@ void gs201_pcie_cp_dump(void);
 static inline int gs201_pcie_cp_poweron(unsigned int speed) { return -ENODEV; }
 static inline void gs201_pcie_cp_poweroff(void) { }
 static inline bool gs201_pcie_cp_link_ok(void) { return false; }
+static inline int gs201_pcie_cp_doorbell(void __iomem *addr, u32 val,
+					 u32 *readback) { return -ENODEV; }
 static inline int gs201_pcie_cp_check_msi_addr(u64 addr) { return -ENODEV; }
 static inline int gs201_pcie_cp_register_queue(irq_handler_t handler,
 					       void *ctx, int *irq)
